Port of _patches/typescript/008-diagnostics-generate.patch (tsc/internal/diagnostics/generate.go) to tsrs.

Go's generator merges effect-tsgo's internal/diagnostics/effectDiagnosticMessages.json (when the file exists) into the
messages it emits. tsrs's generated.rs is produced from Go's output at tsrs's own TypeScript pin, so the Effect
messages are generated by a build script of tsrs_diagnostics instead, from the same JSON:

- build.rs reads ../../../internal/diagnostics/effectDiagnosticMessages.json (the effect-tsgo checkout around tsrs/;
  skipped when missing, as Go skips it), names and keys each message with Go's convertPropertyName, and writes
  $OUT_DIR/effect_generated.rs: one `pub static` per message (Go's identifiers: X_effect_diagnostics_..., ...) and
  EFFECT_MESSAGES, sorted by code. Duplicate codes fail the build, as Go's readRawMessages does.
- lib.rs includes it and re-exports the statics at the crate root, as generated.rs's.
- The key lookup (key_to_message, localize) also covers EFFECT_MESSAGES, as Go's allMessages holds them.
- build-dependency serde_json (to read the JSON).

